Article 31
The provision of services to victims shall be implemented with:
a. Speed;
b. Safety and comfort;
c. Sense of empathy;
d. Non-discrimination;
e. Easy accessibility;
f. No charges imposed; and
g. Guaranteed confidentiality.

Article 18
The community and family have the following obligations and responsibilities:
a. Prevent the occurrence of violence against women and children;
b. Report if violence occurs;
c. Protect victims; and
d. Provide emergency assistance.

Article 10
Exploitation as referred to in Article 5 letter e is caused by:
a. acts that exploit economically or sexually with the intention of benefiting oneself or others;
b. acts with or without the consent of the victim which include but are not limited to prostitution, forced labor or services, slavery or similar practices, oppression, extortion, utilization of physical, sexual, reproductive organs, or unlawfully removing or transplanting organs and/or body tissues or utilizing the labor or ability of a person by another party to obtain benefits both material and immaterial;
and/or
c. all forms of utilization of sexual organs or other body organs of the victim to obtain benefits, including but not limited to all activities of prostitution or sexual abuse

Article 18
The community and family have the following obligations and responsibilities:
a. Prevent the occurrence of violence against women and children;
b. Report if violence occurs;
c. Protect victims; and
d. Provide emergency assistance.

Article 10
Exploitation as referred to in Article 5 letter e is caused by:
a. acts that exploit economically or sexually with the intention of benefiting oneself or others;
b. acts with or without the consent of the victim which include but are not limited to prostitution, forced labor or services, slavery or similar practices, oppression, extortion, utilization of physical, sexual, reproductive organs, or unlawfully removing or transplanting organs and/or body tissues or utilizing the labor or ability of a person by another party to obtain benefits both material and immaterial;
and/or
c. all forms of utilization of sexual organs or other body organs of the victim to obtain benefits, including but not limited to all activities of prostitution or sexual abuse

Article 9
Neglect as referred to in Article 5 letter d is caused by:
a. acts that result in the failure to fulfill the needs of a child properly, whether physical, mental, spiritual or social, committed by parents, guardians, or any other party responsible for their care;
b. acts of deliberately neglecting to maintain, care for, or look after a child as appropriate, committed by parents, guardians, or any other party responsible for their care;
c. acts of neglecting a person within the scope of their household, whereas according to the law applicable to them or due to an agreement or contract they are obligated to provide livelihood, care, or maintenance to that person; and/or
d. acts that result in economic dependence by means of restricting and/or prohibiting proper work inside or outside the home so that the victim is under the control of that person. e. Neglect within the household.

CHAPTER II
PRINCIPLES AND OBJECTIVES
Article 2
The principles of implementing protection for Victims are:
a. Humanity;
b. Respect and fulfillment of victims' rights;
c. Justice and gender equality;
d. Non-discrimination;
e. Best interests of victims; and
f. Empowerment.
